## Decisions

### How should a row's href be built so it no longer depends on the columns a query asked for?

**Background.** `Model.Link(table, row, origin)` in `internal/db/link.go` builds a record's page address (`href`) from cells in the row it's given. For a GROUP it uses `kind` to pick the app (event → When `/e/`, activity → HCA-Team `/v/`, party → Celebrate `/p/`, family/classroom/grade/other → Who?) and `slug`, falling back to `id`, for the last path segment. For a wiki DOCUMENT it uses `parent` and `name`, and for any other document it uses `url`. MCP (`internal/tools/tools.go:179`) and Ask (`internal/ask/turn.go:70`) call it on the row *after* `(columns …)` has trimmed it, so missing cells give a wrong link.

I checked the read policies in `internal/db/policy.go`: every column Link uses (`kind slug parent name url`) can be read by anyone who can read the row. So reading the stored row adds nothing the viewer couldn't already see.

**Real input, from production MCP today:**
- `(from GROUP (where (= id "grp66iuvIijMm6")) (columns name))` → `href: https://who.heliosian.com/groups/grp66iuvIijMm6` (a "Not here" page)
- `(from GROUP (where (= id "grp66iuvIijMm6")) (columns name kind slug))` → `href: https://when.heliosian.com/e/grp66iuvIijMm6`

- (*) Link takes an ID and reads the stored row
  The signature becomes `Link(table, id string, origin)`. It looks the row up in the model (`m.Table(table).Get(id)`), and returns "" when there's no such row. Every caller passes `row["id"]` instead of the row: the 2 above, plus mail (membershipmail, partymail), search, activitytree and partypages, which already pass full stored rows, so their output stays the same. `link_test.go` gets rewritten to use real sample-fixture IDs, because its current rows are made up. For example, it uses `grp00000000041` as an event, but in the fixture that ID is "picnic managers".
  With this, `(columns name)` on Alumni Night gives `https://when.heliosian.com/e/grp66iuvIijMm6`, the same as asking for `kind slug`. One code path, and no caller can hand Link a partial row again.
- ( ) MCP and Ask look up the stored row before calling Link
  `Link` doesn't change. `tools.go` `href` and `ask/turn.go` `href` each do `m.Table(table).Get(row["id"])` and pass that row to it. Alumni Night gives the same `https://when.heliosian.com/e/grp66iuvIijMm6`. But Link still accepts any row, so a new caller holding a trimmed row would bring the bug back.

