### A generated `href` column works, but it needs two more pieces. Should I build it with both?

**How generated columns work today.** Each table's `Generate` func in `internal/db/schema.go` fills cells such as PERSON `name_show` and DOCUMENT `terminal` when the model is built (`buildRows`, `internal/db/model.go:201`). The func sees only that table's rows. An href fits that: a GROUP's needs only its own `kind`, `slug` and `id`, a PERSON's its `id`, and a wiki DOCUMENT's its parent chain, which is in the same table. `Model.Link` would go away, and every caller would read `row["href"]`.

**The two extra pieces:**
1. **The domain.** An href is absolute (`https://when.heliosian.com/…`), and its host depends on `cfg.Domain`: `heliosian.com` in production, `heliosiandev.com:<port>` from `tools/startserver`. The model doesn't know the domain today. `db.NewStore` would take a domain, and the Generate funcs would receive it. That touches the ~8 `NewStore` callers (wiring, mcp/tools/ask/q/import tests, `tools/searchplan`, `tools/loadcheck`).
2. **Always returned, like `id`.** On its own, a generated column is still cut by `(columns …)`. `picked()` and `redact()` in `internal/db/query.go` keep only the listed columns plus `id`, so `(columns name)` would just drop `href` rather than get it wrong. To fix the bug, `href` would be kept beside `id` in every answer. It also gets added to the column read lists for GROUP, DOCUMENT and PERSON in `policy.go`.

**Real input:** production row `grp66iuvIijMm6`, Alumni Night, kind `event`, no slug.

| query | today | generated column, always returned |
|---|---|---|
| `(from GROUP (where (= id "grp66iuvIijMm6")) (columns name))` | `href: https://who.heliosian.com/groups/grp66iuvIijMm6` (Not here) | `href: https://when.heliosian.com/e/grp66iuvIijMm6` |
| `(from GROUP (where (= id "grp66iuvIijMm6")) (columns name kind slug))` | `href: https://when.heliosian.com/e/grp66iuvIijMm6` | same |
| `(from GROUP (where (= kind "event")) (where (= href "https://when.heliosian.com/e/grp66iuvIijMm6")))` | error: no column href | finds Alumni Night |

Mail and page code that wants a path and not a URL (`partypages.go:83` party redirects, `activitytree.go:87`) would take the path from `href` with `url.Parse`.

- (*) Generated column, domain passed to NewStore, always returned beside id
  Everything above. One place builds an href, and every answer carries the right one whatever columns were asked for.
- ( ) Generated column, domain passed to NewStore, returned only when asked for
  Skips the always-returned rule. `(columns name)` on Alumni Night then answers `{id, name}` with no href. MCP and Ask would add `href` to every column list they pass on, which is the same special case moved into two callers.

ian@fc.run answered: of course it would have to be asked for? we don't want magic forced-on-you columns
